Implements the view-reconcile UI and logic that was previously only
documented but never built (see prior correction commit). Matching
logic is reverse-engineered from real T_Reconcile_Base/Scan/Report data
from the legacy Google Sheets system rather than guessed:

- 13-digit barcodes decode to Article+Size ([prefix][Article 7][pad
  "0"][Size 3][check digit]); items are matched by Article+Size, not
  literal barcode.
- Over-scan cap: once accepted scans for an Article+Size reach its
  qty_expected, further scans are rejected (not over-counted) with the
  same rejection-reason wording as the legacy tool.
- Per-scan result is binary (ตรง/ไม่ตรง) but the report is 3-way per
  line (ตรง/ยังไม่ครบ/ยังไม่ได้ยิง), matching T_Reconcile_Report.
- Adds reconcile_history (append-only, written on ปิดงาน) and a
  remark column + nullable barcode on reconcile_items to
  reconcile-schema.sql — re-run it in Supabase to pick up both.

Verified with a headless-browser smoke test (no console errors, XLSX/
Supabase clients load, barcode parser matches real examples, report/
stats rendering matches expected values for a synthetic batch) since
this sandbox can't authenticate against the production Supabase
project. CLAUDE.md documents which parts (the error vs. rejected-scan
split) are inferred rather than confirmed against the legacy system.

